{
    "word": "повелительно",
    "lang_code": "ru",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [],
        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "dc7be361-e5f9-3fdc-a176-a912767b4478",
                "word": "повелительно",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b16b6ae5-edb4-3b6f-8e16-843e5d1ceb9b",
                        "entry_id": "dc7be361-e5f9-3fdc-a176-a912767b4478",
                        "glosses": [
                            "наречие к повелительный; содержа в себе или выражая повеление, приказание"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "adverb"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c38b433-66bd-4fc8-a441-410a55eecb84",
                                "sense_id": "b16b6ae5-edb4-3b6f-8e16-843e5d1ceb9b",
                                "text": "Казалось, кто-то говорил повелительно, другие голоса, напротив, жалобно упрашивали."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "900fa88c-b82f-446f-8806-f118e952fcc8",
                                "sense_id": "b16b6ae5-edb4-3b6f-8e16-843e5d1ceb9b",
                                "text": "― Не мешай же мне, щенок! ― вскрикнул претендент, топая повелительно ножкой."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f1a5cf6-6f47-4093-ae54-144686b2478f",
                                "sense_id": "b16b6ae5-edb4-3b6f-8e16-843e5d1ceb9b",
                                "text": "Вообще обращение англичан с китайцами, да и с другими, особенно подвластными им народами, не то чтоб было жестоко, а повелительно, грубо или холодно-презрительно, так что смотреть больно."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c4c1dd20-9aea-47cd-b26e-7ac90e1d2906",
                        "source_entry_id": "dc7be361-e5f9-3fdc-a176-a912767b4478",
                        "source_sense_id": "b16b6ae5-edb4-3b6f-8e16-843e5d1ceb9b",
                        "target_lang_word": "bossily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bossily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "760aab39-b788-30dd-9107-3676b3344334",
                                        "entry_id": "455242e2-f7ca-37d6-ad78-cd47f23b66aa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a bossy manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc234c83-abe6-410d-ab0b-71d680cc4f31",
                                                "sense_id": "760aab39-b788-30dd-9107-3676b3344334",
                                                "text": "She feels guilty for pampering him, and salves her conscience by bossily ordering him to go and fetch the clothes from the line[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "55f1aced-be33-4d2b-aaf9-86730185bcbb",
                        "source_entry_id": "dc7be361-e5f9-3fdc-a176-a912767b4478",
                        "source_sense_id": "b16b6ae5-edb4-3b6f-8e16-843e5d1ceb9b",
                        "target_lang_word": "imperatively",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "imperatively",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8448f34-8cb8-3dec-b0b1-b11064b12486",
                                        "entry_id": "f259221b-2b7e-3d2a-a19d-c9114b962243",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an imperative manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12a48866-76f0-489e-ab60-4121b204c088",
                                                "sense_id": "d8448f34-8cb8-3dec-b0b1-b11064b12486",
                                                "text": "Improvement is imperatively needed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e36827c4-dce4-4dc4-8d7f-593e894b9c57",
                                                "sense_id": "d8448f34-8cb8-3dec-b0b1-b11064b12486",
                                                "text": "1625, John Donne, Sermon preached 26 April, 1625, in Fifty Sermons, Volume 2, London: M.F., J. Marriot and R. Royston, 1649, Sermon 33, p. 299,\n[…] being a mother, and having the dignity of a Parent upon her, she does not proceed supplicatorily, she does not pray them, nor intreat them, she does not say, I would you would go forth, and I would you would looke out, but it is Egredimini, & videte, imperatively, authoritatively, Do it, you must do it: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd5a0a02-3e67-432e-8598-f72dde75579d",
                                                "sense_id": "d8448f34-8cb8-3dec-b0b1-b11064b12486",
                                                "text": "If a man has been possessed by devils for long enough they will rend him as they leave him, however imperatively they may have been cast out. Ernest did not stay long where he was, for he feared each moment that his father and mother would come out."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a2d1b1b-c697-4f52-8df8-362766d48a45",
                                                "sense_id": "d8448f34-8cb8-3dec-b0b1-b11064b12486",
                                                "text": "The military band happened to be braying operatic selections on the plaza just then, and twice he raised his hand imperatively for silence in order to listen to a favourite passage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "955a98dd-289e-4ce9-b045-17acf9e4f2a2",
                                                "sense_id": "d8448f34-8cb8-3dec-b0b1-b11064b12486",
                                                "text": "— Come here, Tommy, his sister called imperatively, at once! And you, Jacky, for shame to throw poor Tommy in the dirty sand. Wait till I catch you for that."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5f5857b-ed0e-4c2c-961b-aafe3808ccdc",
                                                "sense_id": "d8448f34-8cb8-3dec-b0b1-b11064b12486",
                                                "text": "[…] wedging his tense arm imperatively under mine, Tom Buchanan compelled me from the room as though he were moving a checker to another square."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
